Description: Tools for building, simulating and estimating compartmental,
    physiologically based pharmacokinetic/pharmacodynamic (PBPK/PD) and
    systems biology models. Models are assembled from explicit components
    (compartments, molecules, transports, reactions, equations, observables,
    parameters and dosing) through a pipe-friendly interface with first-class
    physical units based on 'units'. Models are translated into ordinary
    differential equations and simulated efficiently with 'deSolve' or
    'rxode2'; parameters can be estimated by maximum likelihood or, through
    'nlmixr2est', with nonlinear mixed-effects methods. The package aims to
    provide a flexible, modular framework for model building, simulation and
    estimation while keeping the interface simple and intuitive.
